# rule.require.what-why-headers

every named procedure carries a jsdoc header; every code paragraph a one-line comment
```ts
/**
 * .what = generates proposal via feedback loop     // 1 line
 * .why = ensures code quality before review        // up to 3 lines
 * .note = optional caveats
 */
export const proposeCode = async ({ threads }) => {
  // gather feedback
  const result = await runIterateCycle({ threads });

  // expose artifact
  return result.threads.artist.context.stash.art.inflight;
};
```
paragraph comments state intent only, one line. forbidden: multiline `//` comments, vague or redundant comments
scope: required in prod code; expected in tests for setup/assert; exempt for tiny expressions
enforcement: absent .what or .why = blocker
